<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls.FeatureOutcomeBanner"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:local="using:Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls">

    <!--
    Reports, on a feature's overview card, that Winhance could not determine the state of some settings
    inside it - and names them, each as a link straight to that setting. Attaches to the BOTTOM of the
    card so it is unmistakably about that feature: the parent StackPanel spaces its children by 8, so -9
    closes that gap and overlaps the border by 1, top corners squared and bottom left rounded, the same
    join the settings cards use.

    This REPLACED per-outcome info-badge pills. A detection outcome is a fault, not a badge: badges say
    where a value sits relative to our advice, which is optional detail and reasonably hidden behind
    View > InfoBadges. Hiding "1 setting is saved in the wrong format" behind that same toggle was
    backwards - so this is deliberately NOT gated by it.

    SEVERITY IS ALWAYS INFORMATIONAL, and the per-outcome colour lives on each ROW instead. An earlier
    version set the bar's severity to the worst outcome present, which backfired: a feature holding one
    wrong-format and one unrecognized setting turned the whole bar amber, and the eye then went looking
    for amber only - the blue one effectively disappeared. A neutral bar with one coloured row per kind
    shows both at once.

    Rows are built in code rather than by a DataTemplate because each is a single wrapping TextBlock
    whose Inlines mix literal text with Hyperlink runs. A TextBlock wraps natively, which is what keeps a
    long localized setting name from overflowing the card - a horizontal panel of link buttons would not.
    -->
    <Border Visibility="{x:Bind BannerVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" Margin="0,-9,0,0">
        <local:QuietInfoBar
            IsOpen="{x:Bind IsBannerOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
            Severity="Informational"
            Message="{x:Bind BannerMessage, Mode=OneWay}"
            IsClosable="False"
            IsTabStop="True"
            UseSystemFocusVisuals="True"
            CornerRadius="0,0,4,4">
            <StackPanel x:Name="FragmentHost" Spacing="2" Margin="0,0,0,6"/>
        </local:QuietInfoBar>
    </Border>
</UserControl>
